rv  Block destructive shell commands.

Get started
  rv         Open the workspace shell in the current project
  opencode   Launch OpenCode in a workspace sandbox
  workspace  Attach to the persistent workspace host
  setup      Wire host hooks and start rvd
  test       Try a command before it runs
  doctor     Check service, packs, and hosts

Everyday
  explain     Why something was allowed or blocked
  allow-once  Redeem the six-character code from a hook deny
  scan        Session forensics for deny-only findings
  safety      Show or set normal or strict
  blocks      List recent denials
  service     Is rvd running, down, or skewed

Advanced
  packs      List and enable or disable packs
  policy     Show, draft, or share typed rules
  allowlist  Permanent user-layer exceptions
  hook       Host stdin adapter (Pi / Grok / OpenCode / Claude / OpenClaw / Hermes / Codex / Cursor / Antigravity)
  uninstall  Remove rv-owned hooks, config, and LaunchAgent
  operator   Propose and poll identity launches (review required)

Examples
  → rv
  → rv setup
  → rv test 'git reset --hard'
  → rv explain 'rm -rf ~'

Next
  rv setup       Wire hosts and start rvd
  rv help setup  Flags and what setup writes
