Usage
  rv help
  rv help <command>
  rv help service status
Usage
  rv packs [--enabled] [--verbose] [--json]
  rv packs enable <pack>
  rv packs disable <pack>
  rv packs info <pack>

Examples
  → rv packs
  → rv packs enable core.git
Usage
  rv test [--explain] [--json] [--robot] [--plain] [--no-color] <command>

Flags
  --explain   Print explain steps
  --json      Robot JSON on stdout
  --robot     Robot JSON on stdout
  --plain     Disable browse and color
  --no-color  Disable color

Examples
  → rv test 'git reset --hard'
  → rv test --explain 'rm -rf /tmp/x'
Usage
  rv explain [--json] [--robot] [--plain] [--no-color] <command>

Flags
  --json      Robot JSON on stdout
  --robot     Robot JSON on stdout
  --plain     Disable browse and color
  --no-color  Disable color

Examples
  → rv explain 'git reset --hard'
  → rv explain 'git status'
Usage
  rv service
  rv service status

Subcommands
  status  Print whether rvd is running, down, or skewed (default)

Examples
  → rv service
Usage
  rv service status [--json] [--robot] [--plain] [--no-color]

Flags
  --json      key=value lines (same as --robot)
  --robot     key=value lines
  --plain     Disable browse and color
  --no-color  Disable color

Examples
  → rv service status
  → rv service status --robot
Usage
  rv hook [--host <host>]

Flags
  --host <host>  Host codec: grok (default), pi, opencode, claude, openclaw, hermes, codex, cursor, antigravity
Usage
  rv setup [--force] [--json] [--robot] [--plain] [--no-color]

Flags
  --force     Replace occupied owned hooks (backup *.bak)
  --json      One line, no circles (same as --robot)
  --robot     One line, no circles
  --plain     Disable browse and color
  --no-color  Disable color

Examples
  → rv setup
  → rv setup --force
  → rv setup --robot

After setup
  rv test 'git reset --hard'  Prove day-one deny
  rv doctor                   Confirm hosts and service
Usage
  rv uninstall

After uninstall
  rv setup  Re-wire hosts later
  rv help   All commands
Usage
  rv allow-once <code>
  rv allow-once mint -- <command>
  rv allow-once list
  rv allow-once clear

Notes
  redeem  Paste the six-character code from a hook deny on a TTY
  mint    Optional pre-arm; daily unlock is the code already on the deny

Examples
  → rv allow-once a1b2c3
  → rv allow-once mint -- git reset --hard
Usage
  rv scan [sessions] [path] [--host <host>] [--days N] [--all]

Notes
  sessions  Offline host session stores; deny-only findings. Not a repo scanner.

Examples
  → rv scan
  → rv scan sessions ~/.pi
Usage
  rv policy show
  rv policy draft --english <text> [--save]
  rv policy validate
  rv policy export
  rv policy apply

Notes
  draft  Typed gitPush preview. Apple Intelligence when available; otherwise a canned gitPush fixture.

Examples
  → rv policy show
  → rv policy draft --english 'never allow force-push to main'
Usage
  rv allowlist list
  rv allowlist add <rule>
  rv allowlist add-command <command>
  rv allowlist remove <rule>
  rv allowlist validate

Examples
  → rv allowlist list
Usage
  rv safety
  rv safety normal
  rv safety strict

Notes
  normal  File-tool secret paths plus today's shell evaluate
  strict  Also deny ls / test / stat of a catalog path

Examples
  → rv safety
  → rv safety strict
Usage
  rv blocks [--json] [--robot] [--plain] [--no-color]

Flags
  --json      JSON array on stdout
  --robot     JSON array on stdout
  --plain     Disable color
  --no-color  Disable color

Notes
  ledger  Denial-only. Paths replace the home prefix with ~

Examples
  → rv blocks
  → rv blocks --json
